    given-names: "Rob"
    email: "rob@droogdoc.info"
    affiliation: "Independent"
abstract: >
  A proxy that sits between an AI agent and its model API, tries to
  prevent four common failure modes (hallucinated success, runaway
  cost, blast-radius ignorance, malformed tool calls), and does so
  by running requests through a pipeline of eight small "organs" and
  two protocols before letting them reach the model. Built by one
  non-programmer with the help of Claude. Released as Apache-2.0 in
  the hope that people who can actually code will take it further.
keywords:
  - "LLM agents"
  - "AI safety"
  - "guardrails"
  - "reverse proxy"
  - "agent safety"
  - "sandbox simulation"
  - "human in the loop"
